body:
Thanks for tackling the ButtonGroup overflow gap. Approval needs a maintainer to provide or identify the current governing spec for `overflow="menu"`, including when actions collapse, how the overflow trigger is named, and where focus moves when a focused action collapses.

There are also independent implementation blockers:

- the core TypeScript build fails because the Popover `anchorRef` type does not accept the nullable ref passed here;
- collapsed actions do not inherit `isDisabled` from the outer group, so they can remain operable if an open overflow group becomes disabled;
- the `More actions` accessible label is hardcoded rather than localized;
- the new overflow path has no focused test or Storybook story covering collapse, roving focus, focus restoration, disabled propagation, and focus visibility.

[Automated review]

